## Claim
Text: "5G causes COVID-19."
Claim author: Claire Edwards
Claim date: October 25, 2020
Claim origin: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xMLFiRmWSxk

## Initial Q&A
### Is there any peer-reviewed scientific study that demonstrates a causal relationship between 5G radiation and the emergence or transmission of the SARS-CoV-2 virus?
Answer: No, the search result does not provide any peer-reviewed scientific study demonstrating a causal relationship between 5G radiation and the emergence or transmission of SARS-CoV-2. Instead, it cites authoritative bodies such as the International Commission on Non-ionizing Radiation Protection, the World Health Organization, and the U.S. Federal Emergency Management Agency, all of which explicitly state that 5G does not cause COVID-19 or affect its spread.

Source URL: https://www.ucc.org/daily_covid_19_brief_issue_62/

### Has the World Health Organization (WHO) or any other major health authority issued a statement concluding that 5G technology causes COVID-19?
Answer: No, the World Health Organization (WHO) and other major health authorities have not issued a statement concluding that 5G technology causes COVID-19; rather, the WHO stated that "no adverse health effects have been causally linked with exposure to wireless technology," and agencies like FEMA and the FCC have refuted such claims.

Source URL: https://www.ctvnews.ca/health/coronavirus/truth-tracker-no-covid-19-has-nothing-to-do-with-5g-technology-1.4894541

### Were any COVID-19 cases reported in geographic areas that had no 5G network coverage prior to the pandemic's onset in late 2019 or early 2020?
Answer: Yes, the article states that "COVID-19 is spreading in many countries that do not even have a 5G mobile network," indicating that COVID-19 cases were reported in areas without 5G coverage prior to and during the pandemic's onset.

Source URL: https://theconversation.com/conspiracy-theories-about-5g-networks-have-skyrocketed-since-covid-19-139374

### What specific biological mechanism could explain how non-ionizing 5G electromagnetic waves (millimeter waves) produce a viral respiratory disease like COVID-19?
Answer: The search result describes a proposed biological mechanism by which non-ionizing radio frequency electromagnetic waves, such as those used in 5G, could potentially influence viral infections: "radio frequency waves open the calcium channels in the cell membranes and enhance the concentration of free radicals," which "establishes an environment that is particularly favourable for the replication of viruses." It further notes that long-term exposure may repress the immune system, suggesting that such exposure could act as a co-factor accelerating viral replication. However, this mechanism does not demonstrate that 5G causes COVID-19; rather, it hypothesizes that RF exposure might exacerbate existing viral infections by facilitating replication, not that it produces the virus itself.

Source URL: https://www.europarl.europa.eu/doceo/document/P-9-2020-002498_EN.html

### Is the global timeline of 5G deployment consistent with the first reported COVID-19 outbreak in Wuhan, China, in December 2019, given that 5G was already active in many cities by then?
Answer: The timeline is consistent: China officially launched commercial 5G networks in September 2019, months before the first reported COVID-19 outbreak in Wuhan in December 2019, so 5G was already active in many cities by then. However, this consistency does not imply causation.

Source URL: https://www.voanews.com/a/east-asia-pacific_voa-news-china_chinese-5g-not-living-its-hype/6196962.html

### Have any controlled laboratory experiments shown that exposure to 5G frequencies facilitates the replication or mutation of coronaviruses?
Answer: Based on the provided search result, there is no evidence of any controlled laboratory experiments demonstrating that exposure to 5G frequencies facilitates the replication or mutation of coronaviruses. The article discusses a widely debunked and retracted paper that made such claims, but experts described it as "a wacko hypothesis" and "not science," and it was removed from PubMed due to serious methodological flaws.

Source URL: https://medicalxpress.com/news/2020-07-linking-5g-covid-swiftly-debunked.html

### What is the consensus among virologists and infectious disease specialists regarding the claim that 5G causes COVID-19, as expressed in official statements or surveys?
Answer: The consensus among virologists and infectious disease specialists, as reflected in official statements from organizations such as the World Health Organization (WHO) and the U.S. Centers for Disease Control (CDC), is that 5G technology does not cause COVID-19. The source notes that "Electromagnetic field (EMF) exposure from 5G devices does not cause COVID-19, nor does it have any effect on the disease process or health outcomes," and that COVID-19 is caused by a contagious virus spread through physical contact, not by radio waves. No credible surveys or official statements from virologists support a link between 5G and COVID-19.

Source URL: https://www.ucc.org/daily_covid_19_brief_issue_62/

